This transport still sends every reconcile root through the folder-only pin reader. File shares are created without owner-sealed pins and a file IPNS name is not a loaded folder, so `getRecipientPubkeyPins(shareRootIpnsName)` can throw through `requireFolder`; the surrounding reconcile path can also skip the file root at the folder-tree lookup before this transport is used. The lower-level re-mint code has a file-node carve-out, but this web reconcile call does not pass the root kind, so file grants do not get that exemption here. A rotated file share can therefore remain unreconciled from the web owner-reconcile sweep. Pass the root kind through this job, or bypass pin lookup for file roots in the same way the share dialog does.

